{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/c-interoperability","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/cxx-interoperability","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift"],"title":"Language interoperability","generated":true,"anchor":"Language-interoperability"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to call imported functions that are declared in a C header."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift imports any function declared in a C header as a Swift global function.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, consider the following C function declarations:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["int product(int multiplier, int multiplicand);","int quotient(int dividend, int divisor, int *remainder);","","struct Point2D createPoint2D(float x, float y);","float distance(struct Point2D from, struct Point2D to);"],"syntax":"occ","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Here’s how Swift imports them:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["func product(_ multiplier: Int32, _ multiplicand: Int32) -> Int32","func quotient(_ dividend: Int32, _ divisor: Int32, _ remainder: UnsafeMutablePointer<Int32>) -> Int32","","func createPoint2D(_ x: Float, _ y: Float) -> Point2D","func distance(_ from: Point2D, _ to: Point2D) -> Float"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Use a CVaListPointer to Call Variadic Functions","type":"heading","anchor":"Use-a-CVaListPointer-to-Call-Variadic-Functions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In Swift, you can call C variadic functions, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"vasprintf(_:_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", using the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Swift ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/getVaList(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/withVaList(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" functions. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withVaList(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function takes an array of "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CVarArg"},{"type":"text","text":" values and provides a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CVaListPointer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value within the body of a closure parameter, whereas the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getVaList(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" function"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns this value directly. With either function, you pass the resulting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CVaListPointer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value as the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"va_list"},{"type":"text","text":" argument of the C variadic function."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, here’s how to call the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vasprintf(_:_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" function in Swift:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["func swiftprintf(format: String, arguments: CVarArg...) -> String? {","    return withVaList(arguments) { va_list in","        var buffer: UnsafeMutablePointer<Int8>? = nil","        return format.withCString { cString in","            guard vasprintf(&buffer, cString, va_list) != 0 else {","                return nil","            }","","            return String(validatingUTF8: buffer!)","        }","    }","}","print(swiftprintf(format: \"√2 ≅ %g\", arguments: sqrt(2.0))!)","\/\/ Prints \"√2 ≅ 1.41421\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift only imports C variadic functions that use a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"va_list"},{"type":"text","text":" for their arguments."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"C functions that use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"..."},{"type":"text","text":" syntax for variadic arguments are not imported, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"therefore can’t be called using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CVarArg"},{"type":"text","text":" arguments."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Call Functions with Pointer Parameters","level":3,"anchor":"Call-Functions-with-Pointer-Parameters"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whenever possible, Swift avoids giving you direct access to pointers. When importing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"C function parameters, however, Swift maps pointer parameters to standard library"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pointer types. The following tables use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type"},{"type":"text","text":" as a placeholder type name to indicate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"syntax for the mappings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For return types, variables, and arguments, the following mappings apply:"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"C Syntax"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Syntax"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"const Type *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafePointer"},{"type":"text","text":"<Type>"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafeMutablePointer"},{"type":"text","text":"<Type>"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For class types, the following mappings apply:"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"C Syntax"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Syntax"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type * const *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafePointer"},{"type":"text","text":"<"},{"type":"text","text":"Type>"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type * __strong *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafeMutablePointer"},{"type":"text","text":"<"},{"type":"text","text":"Type>"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type **"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AutoreleasingUnsafeMutablePointer"},{"type":"text","text":"<"},{"type":"text","text":"Type>"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For pointers to untyped, raw memory, the following mappings apply:"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"C Syntax"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Syntax"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"const void *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafeRawPointer"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"void *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafeMutableRawPointer"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"C function pointers are imported into Swift as closures with the C function pointer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"calling convention, denoted by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@convention(c)"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute. For example, a function"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pointer that has the type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"int (*)(void)"},{"type":"text","text":" in C is imported into Swift as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@convention(c) () -> Int32"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the type of the value pointed to by a C pointer cannot be represented by Swift,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as is the case with an incomplete struct type, the pointer is imported as an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OpaquePointer"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Standard Library"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Using Imported C Functions in Swift"},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/CVarArg":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CVarArg","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type whose instances can be e